NOTICE
======

This repository contains the artefact for:

    "What Moves a Quantum Advantage? Initialisation, Training Protocol and
     Circuit Ablation in Hybrid Quantum-Classical PINNs"
    NQComp 2027, Paper ID 583.

UPSTREAM WORK THIS STUDY REPLICATES
-----------------------------------

A substantial part of this study is a replication of, and a set of controls
around, the following work, and would not exist without it:

    A. Farea, S. Khan and M. S. Celebi,
    "QCPINN: Quantum-Classical Physics-Informed Neural Networks for Solving
     PDEs", Mach. Learn.: Sci. Technol., 2025; arXiv:2503.16678.

    Code:    https://github.com/afrah/QCPINN
    Commit:  0dc467be8b16cccaa5101e63fe8cdf8d18bfdcb9  (2025-12-15)
    Licence: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Afrah Farea

That code is NOT redistributed here. It is obtained by running
`setup_qcpinn.sh`, which clones the upstream repository at the exact commit
above. All runs in this study that use it ran it UNMODIFIED, in its own pinned
environment, adding only a per-run random seed.

Where this study reports a result for the upstream model, it is a measurement
of their released implementation, not a reimplementation of it. The published
result reproduces: we find no discrepancy with their reported measurement.

SCOPE OF OUR OWN CONTRIBUTION
-----------------------------

Our contribution is the experimental design around that code -- the matched
convergence protocol, the symmetric control, the initialisation and ablation
studies, the third equation, the hyperparameter sweep, the exact statistical
tests, and the verification suites -- together with our own independent
implementation (`qapinn_model.py`, `train.py`, and the `pm_*` runs), which is
architecturally distinct from the upstream model and is described in Table I
of the paper.
